  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with resnet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion. All six completed experiments have used pca_n2000, leaving the RNA encoder choice entirely unexplored in the multimodal setting. The image encoder swap (resnet50 vs ViT-L) yielded only ~0.004 difference, suggesting diminishing returns on that axis, whereas a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200) could capture nonlinear cell-state structure that linear PCA misses. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned variational RNA encoder (scvi_n200) improve multimodal performance when all other components (resnet50, avgpool, weighted) are held at their proven-best settings? Why this is the best next experiment: config_031 is a clean single-variable swap from the current champion, isolating the RNA-encoder effect. The potential upside is large (a learned encoder could unlock meaningful gains over PCA), and a null result would confirm PCA sufficiency, freeing budget to explore other axes. This is more informative than filling in the transformer+weighted cell (config_021), where the expected gain is small given that avgpool already dominates transformer by ~0.04 with concat fusion."
}

